                "retweet_count": 5,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Tonight I voted YES on H.R. 2483, the SUPPORT for Patients and Communities Reauthorization Act. This crucial bill will reauthorize and revise HHS programs addressing substance use disorders, overdoses, and mental health. I am glad to announce that this bill passed the House. Big thank you to my friend, @RepGuthrie for his leadership on this. \n\nThis legislation will be a lifeline for our communities, extending much needed support for vital programs that provide for some of our most at risk populations with prevention, recovery, and resource access. \n\nThe bill also expands resources for first responders, supports employment and transportation services for those in recovery, and establishes new HHS requirements to combat cybersecurity threats, tackle fentanyl contamination, and review critical drug scheduling.\n\nThis is a win for America.",
                "text_lang": "en",
